{
  // Root AGGREGATING tsconfig — NOT used by `pnpm typecheck` (that runs per-package via `pnpm -r exec
  // tsc`, each package's own tsconfig.json), and NOT used by dependency-cruiser (verified 2026-06-26:
  // its resolution + type-only detection are identical with/without it). Its real consumers arrive next:
  // vitest's type lane (the `.test-d.ts` project) and Stryker's typescript-checker (Phase 4) both default
  // tsconfigFile to `tsconfig.json`. Extends the base + widens `include` to the whole graph (the base's
  // `${configDir}/src` would only see a root src/).
  // This aggregator typechecks node-context code (`scripts/` tooling + `tests/` harnesses use
  // `node:*`), so it adds `@types/node` on top of the isomorphic base (`types: []`). This does NOT
  // weaken kit-purity: that is enforced per-package (each package's own `tsconfig` keeps `types: []`)
  // + the dep-cruiser `kit-purity` gate — never by this root config.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  // `allowImportingTsExtensions` MOVED TO THE BASE 2026-08-03 (tsx-shedding stage 1) — it is no longer a
  // `scripts/`-only allowance: every relative import in the repo now carries its extension, because node's
  // type-stripping does not resolve extensionless paths. Kept out of this block deliberately; the base owns it.
  // `jsx`: the aggregator sweeps some JSX (tests/**/*.test-d.tsx if any); per-package jsx stays local.
  // NOTE — the aggregator stays DOM-LESS on purpose: it is a NODE program (server code relies on
  // node's looser `BodyInit`/`BlobPart`, which lib.dom would override and reject `Uint8Array` — the
  // 2026-06-28 incident). So the browser packages are EXCLUDED: `packages/ui/src` + `packages/client/src`
  // (each typechecked with `dom` by its OWN tsconfig via per-package `pnpm typecheck`), the `.ct.tsx` mirror + the CT harness
  // (browser tests — playwright/vite compiles them, never in `pnpm check`; the doctrine). The
  // NODE-side `tests/ui/tokens/*.test.ts` (which imports the node `tokens.build.ts`) stays in here.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["node"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    // BUNDLER here, deliberately, while tsconfig.base.json is nodenext (tsx-shedding stage 4). This
    // aggregator EXCLUDES packages/{ui,client}/src as roots but still pulls them in TRANSITIVELY, and
    // those packages' real resolver is vite. Checking them under node-strict resolution makes tsc pick
    // different third-party declaration files than the ones that actually ship (echarts resolved two ways
    // => phantom type-identity mismatches). NODENEXT ENFORCEMENT LIVES WHERE NODE RUNS: each of
    // packages/{server,kit,contracts,db} is checked under nodenext by its OWN tsconfig via the
    // per-package `pnpm typecheck` — that is the stage-4 guarantee, and it is not weakened here.
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler"
  },
  // Root-level config files JOINED 2026-08-03: they were typechecked by NO program, which let two
  // dead vitest keys (`minWorkers`, `poolOptions` — both removed in Vitest 4) sit silently in
  // vitest.config.ts / vitest.stryker.config.ts across the major bump. Excess-property checking
  // against the installed types is exactly what catches that class. (packages/client/vite.config.ts
  // was already owned by the client program; these are their root-level siblings.)
  // playwright-ct.config.ts is DELIBERATELY absent: @playwright/experimental-ct-react bundles its own
  // vite@6, so its ctViteConfig types collide with our vite@8-typed plugins (tailwindcss()) under
  // exactOptionalPropertyTypes — a dual-vite type world no single program can own honestly. Re-add it
  // the day playwright-ct rides the same vite major.
  // `platform.d.ts` rides beside `reset.d.ts` — the root ambient pair (node-26 adoption program §1.2).
  "include": [
    "packages/*/src",
    "scripts",
    "tooling/src",
    "tests",
    "reset.d.ts",
    "platform.d.ts",
    // AGGREGATOR-ONLY (not in tsconfig.base.json): the `*.css` shorthand for browser asset side-effect
    // imports this program pulls in TRANSITIVELY (ui/src/markdown/math.ts's katex CSS). Never enters a
    // per-package program, so no collision with ui's css-modules.d.ts / client's vite/client.
    "aggregator-assets.d.ts",
    // The PUBLISHED plugin-SDK declaration file (#774) — script-kind, ambient by design (an author drops it
    // next to their main.js). Included HERE, explicitly, because the per-package server program EXCLUDES it
    // (its globals must not leak into server src — see packages/server/tsconfig.json) while the conformance
    // pin `tests/contracts/plugin/host-v1.test-d.ts` needs its globals in THIS program (a /// reference
    // from the test proved unreliable under the vitest typecheck lane — a stale referenced-file view
    // survived cache clears; config-level inclusion resolves freshly).
    "packages/server/src/entry/boot/seed-assets/plugins/host-v1.d.ts",
    "vitest.config.ts",
    "vitest.stryker.config.ts",
    "playwright.config.ts",
    "knip.ts"
  ],
  // Browser tsx under tests/ui, tests/client, and tests/support/ct import `@orb/ui`/`@orb/client` and
  // would drag dom-only source into this node program — exclude the whole browser-tsx SURFACE by
  // DIRECTORY, not by filename suffix. (A mis-named `-fixture.tsx` outlier slipped the old suffix globs
  // and landed here mis-libbed — checked without dom, and never checked WITH it; D62 boundary hardening.)
  // Every `.tsx` in those three trees is browser and owned with dom by ui/client tsconfig. The node-side
  // CT plumbing (`tests/support/ct/*.ts`, e.g. route-trpc.ts) STAYS here (`.ts`, not `.tsx`), as does the
  // node `tests/ui/tokens/*.test.ts`.
  // `__g_*` — the check-gates self-test's reserved throwaway-fixture sentinel (see tsconfig.base.json's
  // exclude note): this aggregator sweeps packages/scripts/tests, so it must skip the sentinel too or a
  // concurrent `typecheck:graph` catches a fixture mid-lifecycle → phantom error.
  "exclude": [
    "packages/ui/src",
    "packages/client/src",
    "tests/ui/**/*.tsx",
    "tests/client/**/*.tsx",
    "tests/support/ct/**/*.tsx",
    "playwright",
    "**/__g_*",
    "**/__g_*/**",
    // Same DOM-barrel hazard: this test value-imports `createFormHandleBridge` from `@orb/client/forms`,
    // which re-exports `use-app-form` and thus every DOM bound-field → phantom lib.dom errors in this
    // DOM-less node program. The bridge SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by packages/client/tsconfig.
    "tests/client/forms/create-form-handle-bridge.test.ts",
    // Same DOM-barrel hazard: value-imports `mirrorDraft`/`readDraftSeed` from `@orb/client/forms`, whose
    // barrel re-exports `use-app-form` and thus every DOM bound-field → phantom lib.dom errors here. The
    // entity-form-base SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by packages/client/tsconfig.
    "tests/client/forms/entity-form-base.test.ts",
    // The draft-store test's subject defaults to window.localStorage (the crash-mirror home) — DOM-coupled
    // `.ts`, so it lives in tsconfig.tests-dom.json (the same routing as its forms siblings above).
    "tests/client/state/create-entity-draft-store.test.ts",
    // Same DOM-barrel hazard, registry flavor: this test value-imports the nine settings-SECTION
    // contributions from the feature front doors (`@orb/client/features/*`) so it can run the DOOR's own
    // `assertSettingsKeyPartition` over the REAL claims — a violated partition throws at main.tsx module
    // init, i.e. a white screen, so the pre-image of that crash belongs in a test. Those front doors are
    // `.tsx` React surfaces → phantom lib.dom errors in this DOM-less node program. The subject SOURCE
    // stays dom-typechecked by packages/client/tsconfig.
    "tests/client/state/config-group-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-partition.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-registry.test.ts",
    // Same class, RAF flavor: the subject hook (`use-message-items`, PD-147) calls bare
    // `requestAnimationFrame`/`cancelAnimationFrame` (lib.dom globals) → phantom lib.dom errors in this
    // DOM-less node program. The hook SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by packages/client/tsconfig.
    "tests/client/features/chat/hooks/use-message-items.test.ts",
    // #1228: same DOM-barrel-hazard class — value-imports `@orb/client/features/chat` (2 pure
    // functions), whose barrel re-exports `chat-list-surface.tsx` (DOM-coupled) → phantom lib.dom
    // errors in this DOM-less node program. The barrel SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by
    // packages/client/tsconfig; this test lives in tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/join-token.test.ts",
    // CT plumbing that is itself DOM-COUPLED: `dropFiles` builds a `DataTransfer` + `File` INSIDE the page
    // (an `evaluateHandle` callback), so its body needs lib.dom even though it is `.ts` node-side glue —
    // the one exception to the "tests/support/ct/*.ts stays here" note above. Home: tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/support/ct/drop-files.ts",
    // Same exception, geometry flavor: the settings render-parity harness measures section boxes INSIDE the
    // page (a `page.evaluate` callback reads `document` + `getBoundingClientRect`), so its body needs
    // lib.dom. Home: tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/support/ct/settings-geometry.ts",
    // Same exception, density-tier flavor: the per-pane tier-liveness probe reads computed font-size off a
    // list row INSIDE the page (a `locator.evaluate` callback: `getComputedStyle` + a throwaway probe node
    // for the token), so its body needs lib.dom. Home: tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/support/ct/tier-liveness.ts",
    // Same DOM-barrel hazard, ui flavor: the waystone MATRIX test is pure data (`waystone-treatment`), but it
    // reaches it through the `@orb/ui/meter` barrel, which value-exports the `<Waystone>` component — and that
    // component subscribes to `document.visibilitychange` (it pauses its ambient layers in a hidden tab). That
    // drags lib.dom globals into this DOM-LESS node program. The SOURCE stays dom-typechecked by
    // packages/ui/tsconfig; this test lives in tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/ui/charts/meter/waystone-treatment.test.ts",
    // The WHOLE e2e tree is DOM-context by ruling (owner, 2026-07-24): playwright specs read browser
    // state inside `page.evaluate` callbacks, and typing them DOM-less forced hand-rolled element-shape
    // bridges + `as unknown as` casts in every spec (the DomEl/DomRow pattern). The tree lives in
    // tsconfig.tests-dom.json (dom + node — its specs are node harness code driving a browser).
    "tests/e2e",
    // The ST-parity probe's captured SillyTavern install (gitignored; `scripts/probes/st-goldens/README.md`).
    // This aggregator `include`s all of `scripts`, and a specified `exclude` REPLACES tsc's default
    // `["node_modules", …]` — so without this line the foreign app's four root `.d.ts` files join the
    // program, and `public/global.d.ts` declares ST's browser globals into OUR global scope. Verified by
    // planting a file: closure hits go 1 → 0. The rig's own five scripts DO typecheck here (2026-08-06);
    // this excludes the third-party runtime beneath them, never our code.
    "scripts/probes/st-goldens/sillytavern-runtime",
    // #1228, the DOM-lib-leak defuse: this script's `page.evaluate` callbacks read `document`/
    // `HTMLElement` inside the browser and formerly carried a program-scoping `/// <reference lib="dom"
    // />` that silently supplied lib.dom to this WHOLE aggregator, masking every other DOM-coupled
    // escapee below. Removed the directive; the script now typechecks under tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "scripts/probes/st-goldens/generate-goldens.ts",
    // Same #1228 leak, ct-support flavor: these `tests/support/ct/*.ts` files reach `document`/
    // `HTMLElement`/`getComputedStyle`/`requestAnimationFrame` inside `page.evaluate`/`locator.evaluate`
    // callbacks — DOM-coupled non-`.tsx` escapees, same class as the pre-existing drop-files/
    // settings-geometry/tier-liveness trio just below. Homed at tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/support/ct/accessible-names.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/autosave-status-transcript.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/canvas-ink.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/held-portrait-image.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/measure-clamp.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/part-vs-surface.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/pixel-contrast.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/scroll-containing-block.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/touch-floor.ts",
    "tests/support/ct/weave-drive.ts",
    // Same #1228 leak, tests/tooling flavor: these int/CT tests drive a REAL chromium directly
    // (`@playwright/test` `chromium.launch`/`@playwright/experimental-ct-react`) rather than importing a
    // package's DOM-typed source, so no other program's reach-back claims them. Homed at
    // tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/tooling/_shared/browser.int.test.ts",
    "tests/tooling/design-audit-walker.ct.tsx",
    "tests/tooling/snap/cascade.suite.int.test.ts",
    "tests/tooling/snap/ops/contrast.int.test.ts",
    // Same #1228 leak, node-fetch-lib flavor: this file's planted `fetch` stand-in types against
    // `RequestInfo` (the whatwg fetch surface tsc sources from lib.dom, not `@types/node`). Homed at
    // tsconfig.tests-dom.json.
    "tests/tooling/stack/lib/engine-launch.test.ts",
    // Same #1228 leak, TRANSITIVE-barrel flavor: this file imports every `@orb/client/features/*`
    // config-group barrel (a non-component sibling of ct-data-providers.tsx, which is ALREADY excluded
    // above and homed at packages/client/tsconfig.json) — a `.ts` file no `.tsx` directory reach-back
    // claims, so its DOM-coupled component chain used to reach dom lib ONLY through the leak. Homed at
    // packages/client/tsconfig.json beside its `.tsx` sibling (its only two consumers are both
    // client-owned; this is the correct home per the ct-data-providers.tsx upward-cake precedent, not
    // the generic tests-dom.json escapee list).
    "tests/support/ct/ct-config-groups.ts",
    // #1243, Arm A-prime — the fork ledger for #1228's residual (types:graph 454/45 → 0/0). Most of the
    // residual was tests bare-importing a client barrel (`@orb/client/{data,lib,state}`) for a pure
    // symbol — those got RE-POINTED at the new `@orb/client/*/pure` subpath
    // (packages/client/src/{data,lib,state}/pure.ts + the package.json exports-map entry), never listed
    // here. These 8 are the residual's OTHER shape: a test that deep-imports a client SOURCE file
    // directly (the pre-existing "Deep import the PURE module, not the barrel" convention) whose OWN
    // code (or whose one needed symbol's OWN file) is genuinely DOM-coupled — no pure surface is
    // possible, so tsconfig.tests-dom.json is their home instead (see its matching comment there).
    "tests/client/data/auth-bootstrap.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/auth-config.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/stale-session.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/message-actions-reveal.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/auth/lib/route-guards.test.ts",
    "tests/client/agent-nav/index.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/character/lib/character-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/preset/lib/preset-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/world-info/lib/entry-draft-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/forms/create-autosave-entity-form-model.test-d.ts",
    // #1243 final leg (owner-accepted plan change, bridge 178): mechanical homing for the tail instead
    // of more pure-surface minting. Same shape as agent-nav above.
    "tests/client/agent-rpg/index.test.ts",
    "tests/client/agent-seed/index.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/workloads-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/portability-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-documents-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/persona/lib/persona-editor-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/discovery/lib/corpus-faces.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-books-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/character/lib/character-card-form-model.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/chat/lib/chat-summary-row.test.ts",
    "tests/client/forms/create-autosave-entity-form-model.test.ts",
    // #1243, pure.ts #lib-trim displacement (see tsconfig.tests-dom.json's matching comment).
    "tests/client/state/active-chat-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/bus/apply-chat-bus-event.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/chat-stream.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/config/lib/config-search.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-group-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-partition.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-section-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/config-teach.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/create-gated-store.test.ts",
    "tests/client/state/create-gated-store.test-d.ts",
    "tests/client/state/assemble-chrome.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/bus/room-registry.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation-carrier.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/invalidation-reads.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/query-client.test.ts",
    "tests/client/data/session-freshness.test.ts",
    // #1243: two more #data-internal-alias reachers found on the re-measure after the pure.ts trim -
    // preflight-warn.ts -> use-refinery-schemas.ts -> "#data", and workloads-schedule-model.ts ->
    // workloads-model.ts -> "#data" (workloads-model.test.ts's OWN import was already homed above, but
    // workloads-schedule-model.ts reaches the SAME impure file via a second, independent test).
    "tests/client/features/refinery/lib/preflight-warn.test.ts",
    "tests/client/features/workloads/lib/workloads-schedule-model.test.ts",
    // #1243: use-orb-socket.ts imports "../stale-session.ts" directly (not via the "#data" alias this
    // time, a plain relative import) which chains to auth-bootstrap.ts/auth-config.ts - the same
    // DOM-coupled data/ files, a fourth independent path to them.
    "tests/client/data/bus/use-orb-socket.test.ts",
    // #1243, packages/ui half: the SAME class as the client escapees above, on the OTHER package.
    // web-weave-*.test.ts bare-import "@orb/ui/web-weave" for pure geometry/physics (buildWeb,
    // WEAVE_TIMELINE, the Weave* types) - a .test.ts, not .tsx, so no packages/ui/tsconfig.json
    // reach-back claims it, and the barrel also carries the DOM-coupled web-weave.tsx component.
    // bar-list/option.test.ts deep-imports charts/bar-list/option.ts, which imports
